      "number": 333196,
      "title": "chat: add customization migration assessment telemetry",
      "url": "https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/pull/333196",
      "baseSha": "fc0a9e94576224c89cc08d390b38ab760a261f1f",
      "headSha": "37e5ee7b1a9747057e9f3d6b4797ce90f27ba6e9",
      "findingCount": 2,
      "published": true,
      "jsonReport": "pr-333196-37e5ee7b1a97.json",
      "markdownReport": "pr-333196-37e5ee7b1a97.md",
      "publishedComments": [
        {
          "path": "src/vs/sessions/services/sessions/browser/sessionsService.ts",
          "line": 789,
          "side": "RIGHT",
          "body": "**[Experimental performance review bot]**\n\n**Severity: medium**\n\nThe added fire-and-forget call invokes `reportCustomizationMigrationTelemetry` after every `_openChat`, including opens of side chats and subagent chats in a session that is already active.\n\nOpening or switching among chats in an already-open Agents session calls `_openChat` each time, so normal tab navigation repeatedly launches the complete customization assessment even though the session lifecycle has not changed.\n\n**Suggested fix:** Move this report to the actual session-entry transition (or guard/deduplicate it by session resource for the current open lifecycle) and leave chat-only navigation free of migration recomputation.\n\n(Written by Copilot)"
        },
        {
          "path": "src/vs/sessions/services/sessions/browser/sessionsService.ts",
          "line": 1614,
          "side": "RIGHT",
          "body": "**[Experimental performance review bot]**\n\n**Severity: medium**\n\nThe new loop fire-and-forgets one `_reportCustomizationMigrationTelemetry` call for every already-resolved restored session without a limiter, idle deferral, or grouping by equivalent assessment scope.\n\nReloading an Agents window with several persisted visible sessions immediately launches a full customization assessment for every restored session just as the workbench is restoring. Different workspace roots prevent MCP-scope coalescing, so a realistic multi-session grid fans out concurrent work.\n\n**Suggested fix:** Queue these reports with bounded concurrency or defer them to idle, and coalesce assessments that share the same session type/workspace scope while preserving the required per-session telemetry semantics.\n\n(Written by Copilot)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 334341,
      "title": "Add opt-in auto-archive inactive sessions with merged pull requests",
      "url": "https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/pull/334341",
      "baseSha": "42b37b7a649d40d17f9e2cf88b94626e0de8269e",
      "headSha": "7e6d14157062b843b8a4ca0efc58f6b2157f306b",
      "findingCount": 1,
      "published": true,
      "jsonReport": "pr-334341-7e6d14157062.json",
      "markdownReport": "pr-334341-7e6d14157062.md",
      "publishedComments": [
        {
          "path": "src/vs/platform/agentHost/node/agentHostSessionLifecycle.ts",
          "line": 144,
          "side": "RIGHT",
          "body": "**[Experimental performance review bot]**\n\n**Severity: medium**\n\nThe new hourly lifecycle restores every due deletion candidate before checking whether its retained worktree makes automatic deletion impossible; rejected candidates remain eligible and repeat the sequence next hour.\n\nAutomatically archived sessions whose worktree cleanup was skipped or failed repeatedly consume GitHub API budget and provider/database I/O every hour despite being unable to make deletion progress.\n\n**Suggested fix:** For delete candidates, run a cheap `canDeleteSession` preflight before the GitHub refresh and restore, while retaining the current in-disposal recheck for race safety.\n\n(Written by Copilot)"
        }
      ]
    }
